    thinking: "**Developing Smart Auto Clicker**\n\nI\'m moving forward with a plan to build a \"Smart Auto Clicker\" app in Kotlin using Jetpack Compose and Material 3 with dark mode. Root access won\'t be required. I\'m focusing on the foundation: utilizing AccessibilityService and dispatchGesture for a range of interactions, including taps, double-clicks, long presses, swipes, and scrolls. I\'ll need to figure out how to incorporate text pasting too.\n\n\n**Adding OCR and Scripting**\n\nI\'ve made progress on integrating OCR using Google ML Kit for text recognition, focusing on on-device processing and Vietnamese/Latin language support. I\'m also planning to use the ClipboardManager for text pasting. I\'m now exploring JavaScript engines like Rhino to run custom scripts, and considering using Java host objects for custom APIs to handle OCR and screen actions.\n\n\n"
