    content: "---\nname: \"room-database-integration\"\ndescription: |\n  Expert assistant for Room Database integration in Android. Provides\n  production-ready code patterns for local data persistence using modern\n  Kotlin, KSP, and Jetpack Compose. Use when the user needs to store data\n  locally (e.g., SQLite, Offline mode, Cache).\n\n  Limitations & Scope Constraints:\n  - Room is a local-only database. It does not support multiplayer, real-time sync, cloud backup and restore, or sharing data across multiple users/devices.\n  - If the user prompt requests cloud-reliant features (e.g., sync, backup and restore, multiplayer) but also specifies Room (or offers Room as an option), you MUST ask the user for clarification before proceeding. Do not silently skip the cloud features or unilaterally switch to another backend.\n---\n\n## Room Persistence Integration\n\nThis skill outlines the steps and best practices for integrating Room Database\nwith modern Android applications.\n\n### Mandates (ALWAYS/NEVER)\n\n-   **ALWAYS use KSP** (Kotlin Symbol Processing) instead of the deprecated\n    KAPT.\n-   **ALWAYS use the Repository Pattern** to abstract data access from the\n    UI/ViewModel.\n-   **ALWAYS return `Flow<T>`** from DAO queries for reactive UI updates.\n-   **ALWAYS mark `insert`, `update`, `delete` as `suspend`** functions.\n-   **NEVER** access the DAO directly from a Composable function.\n-   **NEVER** block the main thread for database operations.\n\n### Setup Checklist\n\n> [!NOTE]\n>\n> In the default AI Studio Android template, Room and KSP are **pre-configured**\n> in `libs.versions.toml` and `app/build.gradle.kts`. If you are working on a\n> default starter template, you can skip the setup checklist and jump straight\n> to **Core Components**.\n\n1.  **Enable KSP Plugin**: Ensure the KSP plugin is applied in\n    `build.gradle.kts` (App level).\n2.  **Add Dependencies**: Use the Version Catalog (`libs.versions.toml`) to add\n    Room dependencies.\n    -   `androidx-room-runtime` -> `libs.androidx.room.runtime`\n    -   `androidx-room-compiler` -> `libs.androidx.room.compiler` (Use with\n        `ksp(...)`)\n    -   `androidx-room-ktx` -> `libs.androidx.room.ktx`\n\n### Core Components\n\n#### 1. Entity (Data Model)\n\nDefine tables using `@Entity`.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Entity\nimport androidx.room.PrimaryKey\n\n@Entity(tableName = \"items\")\ndata class Item(\n    @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Int = 0,\n    val name: String,\n    val timestamp: Long = System.currentTimeMillis()\n)\n```\n\n#### 2. DAO (Data Access Object)\n\nDefine queries and interactions.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Dao\nimport androidx.room.Insert\nimport androidx.room.OnConflictStrategy\nimport androidx.room.Query\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.flow.Flow\n\n@Dao\ninterface ItemDao {\n    @Query(\"SELECT * FROM items ORDER BY timestamp DESC\")\n    fun getAllItems(): Flow<List<Item>>\n\n    @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)\n    suspend fun insertItem(item: Item)\n\n    @Query(\"DELETE FROM items WHERE id = :id\")\n    suspend fun deleteItemById(id: Int)\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Database\n\nAbstract database holder.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Database\nimport androidx.room.RoomDatabase\n\n@Database(entities = [Item::class], version = 1, exportSchema = false)\nabstract class AppDatabase : RoomDatabase() {\n    abstract fun itemDao(): ItemDao\n}\n```\n\n#### 4. Repository (Abstracted Data Source)\n\nIntermediary between DAO and ViewModel.\n\n```kotlin\nclass ItemRepository(private val itemDao: ItemDao) {\n    val allItems: Flow<List<Item>> = itemDao.getAllItems()\n\n    suspend fun insert(item: Item) = itemDao.insertItem(item)\n\n    suspend fun deleteById(id: Int) = itemDao.deleteItemById(id)\n}\n```\n\n### Compose Integration (ViewModel Protocol)\n\n1.  **ViewModel**: Expose data as `StateFlow` and handle actions.\n2.  **UI layer**: Use `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` to observe data reactively\n    and safely.\n\n```kotlin\n// In ViewModel\nval uiState: StateFlow<List<Item>> = repository.allItems\n    .stateIn(\n        scope = viewModelScope,\n        started = SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5000),\n        initialValue = emptyList()\n    )\n\n// In Composable\nval items by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()\n```\n\n### Gotchas & Pitfalls\n\n-   **Missing KSP Plugin**: If you see errors about code generation or missing\n    implementations, double check that the KSP plugin is applied and using the\n    correct syntax in the dependencies block (`ksp(...)`).\n-   **Missing `@Serializable`**: If using Room Entities as Navigation\n    parameters, ensure they are also marked with `@Serializable` and the Kotlin\n    Serialization plugin is applied.\n-   **Thread Safety**: Room handles background execution for `suspend` functions\n    and `Flow` queries automatically, but manual transactions might require\n    explicit dispatcher switching if doing heavy computations before saving.\n"
    raw_content: "---\nname: \"room-database-integration\"\ndescription: |\n  Expert assistant for Room Database integration in Android. Provides\n  production-ready code patterns for local data persistence using modern\n  Kotlin, KSP, and Jetpack Compose. Use when the user needs to store data\n  locally (e.g., SQLite, Offline mode, Cache).\n\n  Limitations & Scope Constraints:\n  - Room is a local-only database. It does not support multiplayer, real-time sync, cloud backup and restore, or sharing data across multiple users/devices.\n  - If the user prompt requests cloud-reliant features (e.g., sync, backup and restore, multiplayer) but also specifies Room (or offers Room as an option), you MUST ask the user for clarification before proceeding. Do not silently skip the cloud features or unilaterally switch to another backend.\n---\n\n## Room Persistence Integration\n\nThis skill outlines the steps and best practices for integrating Room Database\nwith modern Android applications.\n\n### Mandates (ALWAYS/NEVER)\n\n-   **ALWAYS use KSP** (Kotlin Symbol Processing) instead of the deprecated\n    KAPT.\n-   **ALWAYS use the Repository Pattern** to abstract data access from the\n    UI/ViewModel.\n-   **ALWAYS return `Flow<T>`** from DAO queries for reactive UI updates.\n-   **ALWAYS mark `insert`, `update`, `delete` as `suspend`** functions.\n-   **NEVER** access the DAO directly from a Composable function.\n-   **NEVER** block the main thread for database operations.\n\n### Setup Checklist\n\n> [!NOTE]\n>\n> In the default AI Studio Android template, Room and KSP are **pre-configured**\n> in `libs.versions.toml` and `app/build.gradle.kts`. If you are working on a\n> default starter template, you can skip the setup checklist and jump straight\n> to **Core Components**.\n\n1.  **Enable KSP Plugin**: Ensure the KSP plugin is applied in\n    `build.gradle.kts` (App level).\n2.  **Add Dependencies**: Use the Version Catalog (`libs.versions.toml`) to add\n    Room dependencies.\n    -   `androidx-room-runtime` -> `libs.androidx.room.runtime`\n    -   `androidx-room-compiler` -> `libs.androidx.room.compiler` (Use with\n        `ksp(...)`)\n    -   `androidx-room-ktx` -> `libs.androidx.room.ktx`\n\n### Core Components\n\n#### 1. Entity (Data Model)\n\nDefine tables using `@Entity`.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Entity\nimport androidx.room.PrimaryKey\n\n@Entity(tableName = \"items\")\ndata class Item(\n    @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Int = 0,\n    val name: String,\n    val timestamp: Long = System.currentTimeMillis()\n)\n```\n\n#### 2. DAO (Data Access Object)\n\nDefine queries and interactions.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Dao\nimport androidx.room.Insert\nimport androidx.room.OnConflictStrategy\nimport androidx.room.Query\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.flow.Flow\n\n@Dao\ninterface ItemDao {\n    @Query(\"SELECT * FROM items ORDER BY timestamp DESC\")\n    fun getAllItems(): Flow<List<Item>>\n\n    @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)\n    suspend fun insertItem(item: Item)\n\n    @Query(\"DELETE FROM items WHERE id = :id\")\n    suspend fun deleteItemById(id: Int)\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Database\n\nAbstract database holder.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Database\nimport androidx.room.RoomDatabase\n\n@Database(entities = [Item::class], version = 1, exportSchema = false)\nabstract class AppDatabase : RoomDatabase() {\n    abstract fun itemDao(): ItemDao\n}\n```\n\n#### 4. Repository (Abstracted Data Source)\n\nIntermediary between DAO and ViewModel.\n\n```kotlin\nclass ItemRepository(private val itemDao: ItemDao) {\n    val allItems: Flow<List<Item>> = itemDao.getAllItems()\n\n    suspend fun insert(item: Item) = itemDao.insertItem(item)\n\n    suspend fun deleteById(id: Int) = itemDao.deleteItemById(id)\n}\n```\n\n### Compose Integration (ViewModel Protocol)\n\n1.  **ViewModel**: Expose data as `StateFlow` and handle actions.\n2.  **UI layer**: Use `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` to observe data reactively\n    and safely.\n\n```kotlin\n// In ViewModel\nval uiState: StateFlow<List<Item>> = repository.allItems\n    .stateIn(\n        scope = viewModelScope,\n        started = SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5000),\n        initialValue = emptyList()\n    )\n\n// In Composable\nval items by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()\n```\n\n### Gotchas & Pitfalls\n\n-   **Missing KSP Plugin**: If you see errors about code generation or missing\n    implementations, double check that the KSP plugin is applied and using the\n    correct syntax in the dependencies block (`ksp(...)`).\n-   **Missing `@Serializable`**: If using Room Entities as Navigation\n    parameters, ensure they are also marked with `@Serializable` and the Kotlin\n    Serialization plugin is applied.\n-   **Thread Safety**: Room handles background execution for `suspend` functions\n    and `Flow` queries automatically, but manual transactions might require\n    explicit dispatcher switching if doing heavy computations before saving.\n"
