  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/app_icon_generation/SKILL.md"
    end_line: 80
    content: "---\nname: \"app-icon-generation\"\ndescription: >-\n  Instructions for creating and configuring the App Icon for Android apps. Use\n  when you need to create a custom adaptive icon, generate a foreground image,\n  or configure the manifest for the app icon.\n---\n\n# App Icon\n\n## When To Generate\n\n-   **App Icon** \342\200\224 Mandatory for every new app. Replaces the default green\n    Android launcher icon.\n\n## App Icon Implementation\n\nCreate a custom **adaptive icon** following Material You guidelines. This\nreplaces the default launcher icon and must be set up for every new project.\n\n### Tool Usage & Workflow\n\nIf a `generate_image` tool is available, use it to create a custom foreground\nasset representing the app\'s core function instead of writing raw SVG paths.\n\n-   Generate only one foreground icon image related to the app\'s description.\n-   Do NOT use a transparent background color for the generated image.\n\n**Fallback Rule:** If the `generate_image` tool is unavailable or fails (e.g.,\ndue to quota limits), you must manually create a custom Vector Drawable for the\nforeground layer. Choose a bold, filled icon from the core Material Icons\nlibrary that represents the app\'s purpose.\n\n### Requirements\n\n1.  **Foreground layer (`res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml`):**\n\n    -   **Custom Asset:** Do not use basic, thin-lined Material Symbols.\n        Generate a unique, bold, filled vector silhouette or use the generated\n        image asset that represents the app\'s core function for strong visual\n        weight.\n    -   **Implementation:** If using a `generate_image` tool, save the asset as\n        a PNG in `app/src/main/res/drawable/`. **Overwrite the entire file**\n        using a `<layer-list>` to center the asset strictly inside a **66dp**\n        safe zone (within the 108dp canvas):\n\n    ```xml\n    <?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n    <layer-list xmlns:android=\"http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android\">\n        <item\n            android:width=\"66dp\"\n            android:height=\"66dp\"\n            android:drawable=\"@drawable/YOUR_GENERATED_IMAGE_NAME\"\n            android:gravity=\"center\" />\n    </layer-list>\n    ```\n\n2.  **Background layer (`res/drawable/ic_launcher_background.xml`):**\n\n    -   **Palette:** Explicitly avoid the default Android \"Net Green.\" Match the\n        solid background color of your generated image asset, or use a\n        sophisticated brand color scheme.\n    -   **Visual Depth:** Apply a subtle linear gradient (shifting gently\n        diagonally from top-left to bottom-right) between your primary and\n        tertiary theme colors.\n\n3.  **Adaptive wrapper (`res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml` and\n    `ic_launcher_round.xml`):**\n\n    ```xml\n    <?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n    <adaptive-icon xmlns:android=\"http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android\">\n        <background android:drawable=\"@drawable/ic_launcher_background\" />\n        <foreground android:drawable=\"@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground\" />\n    </adaptive-icon>\n    ```\n\n4.  **Manifest:** Ensure `android:icon` and `android:roundIcon` in\n    `AndroidManifest.xml` point to `@mipmap/ic_launcher` and\n    `@mipmap/ic_launcher_round`.\n"
    raw_content: "---\nname: \"app-icon-generation\"\ndescription: >-\n  Instructions for creating and configuring the App Icon for Android apps. Use\n  when you need to create a custom adaptive icon, generate a foreground image,\n  or configure the manifest for the app icon.\n---\n\n# App Icon\n\n## When To Generate\n\n-   **App Icon** \342\200\224 Mandatory for every new app. Replaces the default green\n    Android launcher icon.\n\n## App Icon Implementation\n\nCreate a custom **adaptive icon** following Material You guidelines. This\nreplaces the default launcher icon and must be set up for every new project.\n\n### Tool Usage & Workflow\n\nIf a `generate_image` tool is available, use it to create a custom foreground\nasset representing the app\'s core function instead of writing raw SVG paths.\n\n-   Generate only one foreground icon image related to the app\'s description.\n-   Do NOT use a transparent background color for the generated image.\n\n**Fallback Rule:** If the `generate_image` tool is unavailable or fails (e.g.,\ndue to quota limits), you must manually create a custom Vector Drawable for the\nforeground layer. Choose a bold, filled icon from the core Material Icons\nlibrary that represents the app\'s purpose.\n\n### Requirements\n\n1.  **Foreground layer (`res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml`):**\n\n    -   **Custom Asset:** Do not use basic, thin-lined Material Symbols.\n        Generate a unique, bold, filled vector silhouette or use the generated\n        image asset that represents the app\'s core function for strong visual\n        weight.\n    -   **Implementation:** If using a `generate_image` tool, save the asset as\n        a PNG in `app/src/main/res/drawable/`. **Overwrite the entire file**\n        using a `<layer-list>` to center the asset strictly inside a **66dp**\n        safe zone (within the 108dp canvas):\n\n    ```xml\n    <?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n    <layer-list xmlns:android=\"http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android\">\n        <item\n            android:width=\"66dp\"\n            android:height=\"66dp\"\n            android:drawable=\"@drawable/YOUR_GENERATED_IMAGE_NAME\"\n            android:gravity=\"center\" />\n    </layer-list>\n    ```\n\n2.  **Background layer (`res/drawable/ic_launcher_background.xml`):**\n\n    -   **Palette:** Explicitly avoid the default Android \"Net Green.\" Match the\n        solid background color of your generated image asset, or use a\n        sophisticated brand color scheme.\n    -   **Visual Depth:** Apply a subtle linear gradient (shifting gently\n        diagonally from top-left to bottom-right) between your primary and\n        tertiary theme colors.\n\n3.  **Adaptive wrapper (`res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml` and\n    `ic_launcher_round.xml`):**\n\n    ```xml\n    <?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n    <adaptive-icon xmlns:android=\"http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android\">\n        <background android:drawable=\"@drawable/ic_launcher_background\" />\n        <foreground android:drawable=\"@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground\" />\n    </adaptive-icon>\n    ```\n\n4.  **Manifest:** Ensure `android:icon` and `android:roundIcon` in\n    `AndroidManifest.xml` point to `@mipmap/ic_launcher` and\n    `@mipmap/ic_launcher_round`.\n"
    num_lines: 81
    num_bytes: 3167
  }
}
