  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing the Architecture**\n\nOkay, the icon is done! Now I\'m diving into the Smart Auto Clicker\'s architecture. I\'ve got the Accessibility Service identified as the key component, specifically `SmartAccessibilityService`. This thing will handle gesture dispatch, mainly clicks and taps by sending down and up events with the necessary duration.\n\n\n**Defining Gesture Functionality**\n\nI\'m now detailing the individual gesture capabilities. I\'ve broken it down to double clicks, long presses, swipes, scrolls, and text pasting, each with parameters. I\'m also planning to implement volume key hotkeys for easy start/stop functionality. Finally, I\'m figuring out how to make a single instance of the service, so both the app and the runner can control it effectively.\n\n\n**Optimizing OCR & Overlay**\n\nI\'ve been working on the `SmartOcrManager`. I\'m using Google ML Kit and want to manage resources well with downscaling to avoid memory leaks. I\'ve also detailed the `OverlayService`, which needs the `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` permission. I\'m building a movable widget with a start/stop button, pick point and region selectors, and an open app button. A coordinate picker is also included for precise selections.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Features**\n\nI\'ve sketched out the ROI selector overlay, designed to draw bounding boxes directly on a transparent canvas, capturing precise box coordinates. I\'ve also incorporated a Quick Settings Tile Service, specifically `SmartClickerTileService`, to allow start/stop toggling directly from the Android Notification Quick Settings panel.\n\n\n**Developing Macro Execution**\n\nNow I\'m digging into the macro runner and builder functionality. I\'m visualizing a step-by-step macro config with various step types, like clicks (with jitter and delay), OCR waits, and text pastes. Loop count, interval, and error handling are configurable too. I\'m also implementing real-time logging to the `LogRepository`, and there\'s a failsafe limit check with a flag check in sleep.\n\n**Establishing Database Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the database structure using Room. I\'m focusing on entities for target points, ROI regions, macros (as JSON), and JavaScript scripts. I\'m planning JSON import/export for configs and scripts and to seed the database with the five required sample scripts. I\'ve designed the various entities and their properties.\n\n\n**Designing Advanced Macros**\n\nI\'m now detailing some advanced macro functionality. I\'m focusing on automating actions like automatically pressing a \"Skip\" button when it appears, pasting text and clicking \"Send,\" and creating loops with conditional exits based on text detection or iteration count. I\'m also planning to handle unexpected popups by closing ads or alerts, and implement retry logic with limits for text detection failures. Finally, I\'m designing a new modern Jetpack Compose UI with Material 3 and dark mode support.\n\n\n**Implementing Script Management**\n\nI\'ve moved on to integrating the script writing functionality. The JS editor is coming together on Tab 3, featuring a script list, creation options, and the five sample scripts. The code editor has a user-friendly interface with API shortcut buttons for quick insertion. I\'ve included \"Run,\" \"Stop,\" \"Save,\" and \"Export\" buttons, to allow users to fully test scripts. Furthermore, I\'ve designed Tabs 4 and 5 for points & ROI management, and real-time logging, respectively. Finally, I\'ve also detailed the \"Guide & Known Limitations\" section, covering permission instructions and limitations. I\'ve also updated the `AndroidManifest.xml` to request relevant permissions.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
