  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Overlay Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently diving into the specifics of implementing the Floating Control Button, focusing on the core requirement of using WindowManager with TYPE_APPLICATION_OVERLAY. This involves a detailed look at how to achieve the overlay functionality to meet the user\'s need.\n\n\n**Implementing Floating Features**\n\nI\'ve been concentrating on the implementation of a persistent floating bubble. I plan to use a foreground service to keep it alive. The UI will be a compact, circular bubble, possibly semi-transparent, with a main button and secondary controls on expansion. I\'m focusing on user interaction, so I\'m designing drag-and-drop mechanics to include screen-edge snapping and persistent positioning via SharedPreferences.\n\n\n**Refining Exclusion Strategies**\n\nI\'m now refining how the bubble interacts with screen capture and OCR. I\'ve developed approaches to temporarily hide it during captures using alpha or removing it from the view hierarchy. Additionally, I\'m exploring filtering the bubble\'s rectangle from OCR results. For accidental clicks, I\'ll prevent clicks within the bubble\'s bounds via the `SmartAccessibilityService`. Even better, I\'ll temporarily hide it for capture, then restore it! I\'m also planning a border ring status indicator on the bubble, with colors representing ready, running, and paused states, as well as a counter.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 833208280
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
