  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI Handling**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on the `captureCurrentFrame()` function and how to improve screenshot capture for OCR and scripting. I\'m thinking of adding a call to `ExecutionManager.onTemporarilyHideBubble?.invoke(true)` before the screenshot. I\'m also considering a short wait (50-80ms) to ensure the UI updates, or simply setting the bubble alpha to zero for a more immediate hide.\n\n\n**Refining Safety Measures**\n\nI\'ve made progress on ensuring the floating bubble doesn\'t interfere. I\'m implementing a filter in `OcrEngine.kt` to exclude any `OcrElement` overlapping `ExecutionManager.floatingBubbleRect`. Also, in `SmartAccessibilityService.kt`, clicks within the bubble\'s area will be rejected or jittered, preventing accidental interactions. Hiding the bubble via `alpha = 0f` further ensures OCR exclusion. I\'m now moving on to designing `FloatingControlService.kt` with a foreground service and window manager layout.\n\n\n**Designing Bubble UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the UI of the floating bubble. It will be a 56dp circular element, using `PixelFormat.TRANSLUCENT` for transparency. I will use `SharedPreferences` to remember its position (`PREF_BUBBLE_X`, `PREF_BUBBLE_Y`). For the appearance, I\'m thinking of a semi-transparent dark background with a colored outer border ring that indicates the state (green for idle, red for running, amber/yellow for paused). The central icon will switch between play/stop, and a badge will display loop count or elapsed time. Expansion will reveal a toolbar with pause/resume, point picker, ROI picker, app open, and close buttons.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 64575608
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
