  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Floating Service**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in building the `FloatingControlService.kt`. I\'m meticulously verifying all requirements, especially the use of `WindowManager` with `TYPE_APPLICATION_OVERLAY` for the overlay window, which requires `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` permission. I\'m making sure it runs within the correct context.\n\n\n**Designing Visual Elements**\n\nI\'ve been sketching out the visual components. I\'m aiming for a circular bubble (52-56dp) with a semi-transparent dark background, which will house the main Play/Stop button. Its icon will change to reflect its state: green for idle, red when running, and amber when paused. I\'m also planning the expandable toolbar, which opens on touch or long-press, to include buttons for pause/resume, point picking, ROI picking, opening the app, and closing the bubble.\n\n\n**Implementing Interaction Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dynamic behavior. I\'m building out the interaction between the bubble and the `ExecutionManager`. Specifically, I\'m working on how it registers with `onTemporarilyHideBubble`, updates the `floatingBubbleRect`, and resets when removed. The border ring status indicators and badge display, displaying loop and time information, are getting attention.\n\n\n\n"
