  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Script Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on connecting a floating button to a script within the application. The system will store a list of saved scripts. The user will select one as the \"active script,\" with its name appearing on the button. The goal is seamless script activation via the floating button interface.\n\n\n**Implementing Script Control**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating script control with the floating button. Clicking \"Play\" executes the active script in a separate coroutine within a foreground service, with \"Stop\" immediately halting it. The button\'s extension will offer a \"Change Script\" option. The button will revert to \"Play\" with a toast on script completion or error, and prevent overlapping executions. Finally, I\'ll temporarily hide the floating button during screen captures for OCR accuracy, ensuring it reappears after each capture step.\n\n\n**Refining Script Execution**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring that the selected `script_id` persists by storing it in SharedPreferences or the AppRepository. I\'ve designed `ExecutionManager.startActiveScript(context)` to prevent overlapping jobs, starting the active script in a dedicated Coroutine if it\'s not already running. Upon completion or stopping, it\'ll display a toast message and update the execution status.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 708784824
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
