  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Implementation**\n\nI\'m deep in analyzing the first requirement, the saved script list and active script selection. The goal is to design the exact implementation details. I\'m focusing on the user interface and how the \"active script\" state will be managed and displayed within the application.\n\n\n**Defining Active Script State**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the `activeScript` state using `StateFlow` within the `ExecutionManager`. I\'ve added persistence using `SharedPreferences`, which will store `active_script_id`. The plan is to handle loading the active script at startup and during script loads, as well as providing methods for setting the active script. I\'m focusing on UI elements in `HomeScreen.kt` to show active script info and manage its state, and adding a toggle in `ScriptEditorScreen.kt`.\n\n\n**Investigating Button Actions**\n\nI\'m now investigating what happens when the user interacts with the floating control button (`FloatingControlService`). I\'m looking into the `togglePlayPause()` method within `ExecutionManager` and how it handles different states: idle, running, and paused. I need to understand how the `stop()` method works to cancel the `activeJob` properly, especially to ensure it stops script execution immediately, even if it\'s sleeping or in a loop. I will focus on `ScriptRunner.kt` next.\n\n\n"
