  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI placement**\n\nOkay, I\'m thinking about the UI layout in `HomeScreen.kt`. The idea of putting a dedicated \"Active Script\" card right after the status card, or maybe as a floating button, seems like a good fit. This addresses the user\'s initial request perfectly.\n\n\n**Designing Active Script Display**\n\nOkay, I\'ve just fleshed out the design for the \"Script \304\221ang ho\341\272\241t \304\221\341\273\231ng\" section in `HomeScreen.kt`. I\'m picturing a card with a clear header including an icon and a title. The content will adapt based on whether an active script is selected, displaying its name and description or a placeholder message. I\'m also including \"\304\220\341\273\225i script\" and \"Ch\341\272\241y script n\303\240y\" action buttons within the card, with dynamic display based on script status.\n\n\n**Implementing Script Controls**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating script controls. Specifically, I\'m adding a \"\342\226\266 Ch\341\272\241y script n\303\240y\" button to `ScriptEditorScreen.kt`. If a script is active, a badge shows `[\342\234\223 \304\220ang ho\341\272\241t \304\221\341\273\231ng]`. Otherwise, a `[\342\255\220 \304\220\341\272\267t l\303\240m script ho\341\272\241t \304\221\341\273\231ng]` button is displayed. I\'m also including the active script\'s name in the expanded floating control toolbar, along with a \"\304\220\341\273\225i script\" button to launch a quick script picker. I am aiming to use an overlay view for the picker, allowing for selection from a list of saved scripts.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 254014959
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
