  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Controls**\n\nI\'m impressed by the elegant structure of `FloatingControlService.kt`. Currently, `expandedToolbar` displays a set of controls: Pause, Point picker, ROI picker, Open main app, and Close. I\'m focusing on their layout and functionality.\n\n\n**Expanding the Toolbar**\n\nI\'m now integrating a text label, `activeScriptText`, into the `expandedToolbar` to display the active script, updating it via `ExecutionManager.activeScript`. A \"\304\220\341\273\225i script\" button will trigger `showScriptSelectorOverlay()`, which will allow the user to select scripts from the database and set the active script, updating the text label accordingly. This directly addresses the first requirement regarding script selection. I\'m also ensuring the floating bubble can run the newly selected script!\n\n\n**Implementing Script Interaction**\n\nI\'ve outlined how the user interacts with scripts through new UI elements. A \"Script \304\221ang ho\341\272\241t \304\221\341\273\231ng\" card in `HomeScreen.kt`, a status badge in `ScriptEditorScreen.kt`, and the `\360\237\223\234 [T\303\252n script]` label in the toolbar will provide active script information. I\'ve also implemented the \"\304\220\341\273\225i script\" button to select and update active scripts. The floating bubble\'s Play/Stop functionality, in `FloatingControlService.kt`, calls `ExecutionManager.togglePlayPause(this)` to start, or `stop()` to interrupt, the selected script.\n\n\n**Refining Stop Functionality**\n\nI\'ve refined the script stopping mechanism. Now, `runningThread?.interrupt()` cancels `activeJob?.cancel()` and sets `executionStatus` to IDLE. In `ScriptRunner.kt`, I\'ve implemented a `CancellableContextFactory` that checks for `executionStatus == IDLE` every 50 instructions in `observeInstructionCount`, throwing a runtime exception. The `sleep(ms)` function checks for cancellation at 50ms intervals, ensuring immediate stopping during loops.\n\n**Enhancing Script Selection**\n\nI\'ve added the \"\304\220\341\273\225i script\" button, styled with the `\360\237\224\204 \304\220\341\273\225i` icon, to the expanded toolbar. Clicking this button now triggers the `showScriptSelectorOverlay()` function. This presents a floating dialog showing all saved scripts allowing for immediate script selection without opening the main app.\n\n**Confirming Script Status**\n\nI\'ve ensured that, upon calling stop() or script completion, the floating button automatically reverts to the \"Play\" state (green). I\'m also implementing the displaying of either a \"Script \304\221\303\243 xong\" toast message or an error notification to provide feedback on script status.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 553204088
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
