  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Active Script**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating a new `activeScript` property within `ExecutionManager.kt`. This involves incorporating a `StateFlow<ScriptEntity?>` to manage the active script\'s state and implementing `setActiveScript` to update and persist the script ID to `smart_clicker_prefs`.\n\n\n**Implementing Script Management**\n\nI\'ve integrated logging and status updates when a script is chosen, confirming the active script selection, and updating the UI accordingly. I\'ve also added an initialization function to set up an observer for the script repository, handling cases where there is or isn\'t a script saved in preferences. Finally, I\'ve implemented logic to prevent starting multiple scripts simultaneously, checking for active execution states and confirming a script selection.\n\n\n**Refining Script Execution**\n\nI\'ve been solidifying script execution logic.  I now have added safeguards against duplicate runs and returning if one is in progress, along with handling the assignment to the active script. I\'ve also implemented more robust error catching, differentiating between user stops, script completions, and exceptions, with specific messages and UI updates.  The finalization of the logic also includes cleaning up thread references and cancelling jobs. Finally, I\'m integrating the stop and togglePlayPause functions, with their updated UI and thread management.\n\n\n**Adding Cancellation to Script**\n\nI\'m now incorporating cancellation logic into `ScriptRunner.kt` using a `CancellableContextFactory`. This includes instruction observation within the Rhino context to detect user stops, throwing an exception to halt script execution. I\'ve also integrated cancellation checks into `ScriptApi.sleep` to ensure responsive stopping of scripts.\n\n\n**Implementing Script Stops**\n\nI\'ve integrated the `ScriptApi.stop()` function to invoke `ExecutionManager.stop()`, and now included the appropriate exception to halt the script. I\'ve also added cancellation checks in `ScriptApi.checkCancelled()`, which now actively throws exceptions if the execution status is idle or paused. This handles cases where the user directly stops a script or pauses it via the UI, ensuring smooth interruption.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 655831327
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
