  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Toolbar Elements**\n\nI\'ve been figuring out the toolbar elements. I\'ve got a button for pausing, and I\'m thinking of an active script badge or button displaying the script\'s name, ideally with a max width and ellipsis. There\'s also a button to trigger the script selector overlay and a point picker icon in mind.\n\n\n**Expanding UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the ROI picker `\360\237\224\262`, an open main app button `\342\232\231`, and a close floating button `\342\234\226`. I\'m also examining how `showScriptSelectorOverlay()` functions, focusing on overlay window parameters to ensure proper display, and have started looking into using the proper layout types.\n\n\n**Designing Overlay Elements**\n\nI\'m working on the overlay now, specifically the UI elements within it. I\'ve started on a `LinearLayout` with a rounded background, including padding and elevation. The `FrameLayout`\'s layout parameters dictate the dialog\'s width relative to the screen size. I\'m focusing on preventing click-through on the background. Currently, I\'m integrating a header layout for the title and a close button.\n\n\n**Constructing Selector Overlay**\n\nI\'m now building the script selector overlay\'s elements. I\'ve added a header layout with a title and close button, styled with padding and a gray color. Below that, there\'s a subtitle with explanatory text. Next, a scroll view containing a vertical linear layout for the script list is being implemented. I\'m focusing on the dimensions and layout of these components. I\'ll load the scripts from the Room database into this list later.\n\n\n**Implementing Script List**\n\nI\'m now populating the script selector with content. I\'ve integrated a check for an empty database, displaying a \"no scripts\" message if needed. Otherwise, I\'m iterating through the scripts, constructing a layout for each one. I\'m focusing on the layout params of each script item in the list, including active status, padding, and UI elements.\n\n\n**Refining List Item Layout**\n\nI\'m now refining the layout for each item in the script list. I\'ve focused on styling the list items. These updates involve dynamically creating a background gradient drawable with rounded corners. The background color varies based on whether the script is active, and I\'ve also implemented a stroke to indicate active status. I\'m carefully setting the layout parameters, including margins, and now handling click listeners to trigger the active script and dismiss the overlay. I\'m now working to add the name row.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 272807869
    }
