    thinking: "**Examining Data Collection**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how data is collected in `HomeScreen.kt`. I\'ve identified the use of `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` for both `activeScript` and `allScripts`, indicating active script and all scripts data collection respectively. Both `ExecutionManager.activeScript` and `repository.allScripts` are involved.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m thinking about adding a dedicated card to `HomeScreen.kt`. This card will display the currently active script when the play/stop floating toggle is pressed. It will be positioned either between the status card and the floating toggle card or directly after the floating toggle card in the layout. I\'m exploring the use of a `Card` composable with `Column` and `Row` for structuring the content, and using icons and text to display information related to the active script.\n\n\n**Designing Active Script Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for the active script display within the card. It looks like it is going to display the script\'s name and description. The composable structure will leverage a `Row` to align title and tag, followed by a `Column` for a concise and informative layout. The visual design focuses on clear differentiation when there is no script selected to ensure usability.\n\n\n**Adding Script Picker**\n\nI\'m now integrating a script picker using an `AlertDialog`.  This picker is triggered by an `OutlinedButton`. The picker leverages a `Column` with a `verticalScroll` modifier, allowing for a long list of available scripts. Each script is represented as a `Surface` with a `clickable` modifier and a visual indicator for the selected script. It handles empty library states gracefully with informative text.\n\n\n"
